# Cloudflare Pages redirects — SPA fallback for dynamic routes.
#
# The Next.js static export emits one placeholder HTML page per dynamic
# route (e.g. /qbank/_/index.html). These rules serve that placeholder
# for ANY value in the dynamic segment, so the client-side router can
# pick up the URL and load the actual content from the Worker.
#
# IMPORTANT — two redirect-engine quirks that must be avoided
#
# 1. Infinite-loop detection
#    Cloudflare Pages strips `.html` / `/index` from the destination URL
#    before re-evaluating it against the source pattern. If the destination
#    path matches the source pattern, Pages flags the rule as an infinite
#    loop and SILENTLY IGNORES it — every dynamic URL then returns 404.
#
# 2. Clean-URL 308 redirects
#    If the destination is a `name.html` file, Pages 308-redirects to the
#    clean URL `name` (stripping `.html`), which breaks the `200` rewrite
#    semantics. Directory-style destinations (`name/index.html`) are
#    already "clean" and are served directly without a redirect.
#
# THE FIX
#
# The post-build script `scripts/copy-spa-placeholders.js` copies each
# placeholder HTML to `/_spa/<name>/index.html` — a top-level directory
# whose URL does NOT match any source pattern. The rules below point at
# those directory paths. Run `npm run build` to regenerate the copies
# after each build.
#
# Cloudflare Pages serves real files BEFORE applying redirects, so
# known paths (e.g. /settings/account/ which has its own index.html,
# or /admin/content/raw/) are served directly. Only unmatched paths
# fall through to these rules.
#
# The 200 status (not 301/302) means Cloudflare Pages serves the file
# content at the requested URL — the browser URL stays the same and the
# client router takes over.

# App dynamic routes — placeholder shell for any UID/article/video.
/qbank/*           /_spa/qbank/           200
/flashcards/*      /_spa/flashcards/      200
/osce/*            /_spa/osce/            200
/library/*         /_spa/library/         200
/videos/*          /_spa/videos/          200
/settings/*        /_spa/settings/        200

# Admin dynamic routes — UUIDs not known at build time.
/admin/users/*     /_spa/admin-users/     200
/admin/content/*   /_spa/admin-content/   200
/admin/review/*    /_spa/admin-review/    200

# No catch-all rule.
#
# Cloudflare Pages automatically serves /404.html with HTTP 404 for any
# URL that doesn't match a static file or a redirect rule above. We do
# NOT add `/*  /404.html  404` here because:
#   1. `404` is not a valid redirect status code (valid: 200, 301, 302,
#      303, 307, 308). The rule would be silently ignored.
#   2. Even with status 200, a catch-all would mask real 404s by serving
#      the 404 page with HTTP 200, which is bad for SEO and monitoring.
#
# Next.js's static export generates /404.html automatically; Pages picks
# it up for any unmatched request.
